{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useKeyHold(key): Ref<boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L51","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useKeyHold.ts:51"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable that returns a reactive ref indicating whether a specific key is currently being held."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This composable uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IndividualKey"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Ref"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive ref that is true if the key is currently held down"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div :style=\"{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }\">\n    {{ isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift' }}\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\nconst shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\nconst alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Ctrl</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Shift</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Alt</span>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"key","text":"key","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useKeyHold(key): Ref<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useKeyHold.ts:51](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L51)\n\nVue composable that returns a reactive ref indicating whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis composable uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/vue-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`IndividualKey`\\>\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')\n\n## Returns\n\n`Ref`\\<`boolean`\\>\n\nReactive ref that is true if the key is currently held down\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div :style=\"{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }\">\n    {{ isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift' }}\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\nconst shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\nconst alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Ctrl</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Shift</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Alt</span>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useKeyHold\ntitle: useKeyHold\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useKeyHold(key): Ref<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useKeyHold.ts:51](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useKeyHold.ts#L51)\n\nVue composable that returns a reactive ref indicating whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis composable uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/vue-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if\nthe specified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`IndividualKey`\\>\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A')\n\n## Returns\n\n`Ref`\\<`boolean`\\>\n\nReactive ref that is true if the key is currently held down\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst isShiftHeld = useKeyHold('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div :style=\"{ opacity: isShiftHeld ? 1 : 0.5 }\">\n    {{ isShiftHeld ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift' }}\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useKeyHold } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst ctrl = useKeyHold('Control')\nconst shift = useKeyHold('Shift')\nconst alt = useKeyHold('Alt')\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: ctrl ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Ctrl</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: shift ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Shift</span>\n    <span :style=\"{ opacity: alt ? 1 : 0.3 }\">Alt</span>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n"}
